'''Concepción''' ({{Lang-arn|Huerquehue}}; {{Literal translation|the messenger's place}}), officially '''Concepción del Novèl Extrèm''' ({{Literal translation|beginning of the new extreme}}) is the administrative seat of [[Cadaqués]], the most populous city in [[Cerdanya]], and the [[List of cities in Balisca by population|fourth-most populous]] city in [[Balisca]] with a recorded population of 4,731,571 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. Current to 2025 as well, the [[Greater Concepción Area]] (GCA) held a population of 7,399,662, making it Balisca's [[List of census metropolitan areas and agglomerations in Balisca|fourth most-populous metropolitan area]]. It is located on the southern shore of [[Sea of Shuainia]] directly opposite of the [[Axarquía]] metropolis, and is eastern anchor of the Northern Cerdanyan [[Megaregions of Balisca|urban agglomeration]] known as ''[[Mercepción]]''.

Historically home to the [[w:Mapuche people|Wallche]] and [[w:Yaghan people|Yamana]] indigenous peoples, Concepción was claimed by Beron and Volisanian-speaking [[Catharism|Cathars]] expelled from [[Estuaria]], on behalf of the [[United Kingdoms of Volisanian#Berona|Council of Berona]] in 1616 along with the rest of what would become [[Cerdanya]]. The city was officially founded on 11 May 1616, by [[W:Cathar Perfect|Cathar Perfect]] [[Jacint Guillamó]]. In 1808, Concepción sent delegates to the [[Granyana Convention]], which resulted in the establishment of the [[Northern Confederation]]. In the second half of 19th century Concepción played an important geopolitical role as the it served as a major stopover for ships traveling between the [[Aethiopian Ocean|Aethiopian]] and [[Shendan Ocean|Shendan]] oceans by crossing the Sea of Shuainia between the Shendan and Aethiopian oceans. Concepción rapidly expanded during its golden age, aided by the [[Cerdanya gold rush|Cerdanyan Gold Rush]] and the accompanying influx of immigrants. The gold rush intensified the [[Tinguiririca conflict]] with the Wallche, and was ultimately ended with the [[1883 Confederal Convention]].

Concepción's high density of colleges and universities make it a regional center of higher education including law, medicine, engineering, and business, and the city is considered to be a world leader in innovation and entrepreneurship, with nearly 2,000 [[W:Platform cooperative|platform cooperatives]]. Concepción is an [[Adonia Globalization and World Cities Ranks|Alpha global city]] of culture, politics, media and science. Its economy is based on [[w:High tech|high-tech]] firms and the {{W|service sector}}, encompassing a diverse range of {{W|creative industries}}, research facilities, media corporations and convention venues. Concepción serves as a hub for air and rail traffic and has a highly complex public transportation network. The metropolis is a popular [[Tourism in Balisca|tourist destination]]. Significant industries also include [[w:information technology|IT]], [[w:Medication|pharmaceuticals]], [[W:Biomedical engineering|biomedical engineering]], [[w:Clean technology|clean tech]], {{W|biotechnology}}, {{W|construction}} and {{W|electronics}}.

Concepción is recognized as one of the most [[w:Multicultural|multicultural]] and [[w:cosmopolitanism|cosmopolitan]] cities in the world. Institutions rank among the top in the country for environmental sustainability and [[W:Doughnut economics|doughnut economics]]. The city has one of the highest [[Balisca Consumer Price Index|consumer price indices]] in Balisca as it undergoes widespread redevelopment as part of the [[Casajuan Plan]], though it remains high on world livability rankings. It is additionally known for its cool summers, fog, steep rolling hills, [[Architecture of Concepción|eclectic mix of architecture]], and landmarks.

