==Demographics==
{{Main|Demographics of Concepción}}

{{See also|Demographics of Balisca}}Because of its pre-eminence as a port in the [[Northern Hemisphere]], Concepción has always been one of the main gateways into Balisca. This has attracted many immigrants and made Concepción a cosmopolitan {{W|melting pot}}. By the end of the 18th century about half the population originated from elsewhere in Balisca mostly and also from Cerdanya.

Economic conditions and political unrest in [[Illypno-Fosia]] and the rest of the world brought several other waves of immigrants during the 20th century: Beron immigrants started arriving at the end of the 19th century and in the first half of the 20th century, up to 40% of the city's population was of Beron origin; [[Ukrainian Baliscans|Kalinovans]] from 1917; Armenians in 1915 and 1923; [[Jade Baliscans|Jade]] and [[Sanese Baliscans|Sanese]] and in the 1920s; Breislandic during the 1920s and 1930s; other [[Volisan Baliscans|Volisans]] after 1936; [[Central Kaftia|Central Kaftians]] (both [[Bayani Baliscans|Bayani]] and [[W:Berber people|Imfezzan]]) in the inter-war period; and [[Sudanese Kaftia|Sudanese Kaftians]] after 1945. 

Currently, over one third of the population of Concepción can trace their ancestry back to [[Fosia]]. Concepción also has the second-largest Okataian, [[Barausian Baliscans|Barausian]] and [[Kemali Baliscans|Kemali]] populations of Balisca. Other significant communities include [[Vasari Baliscans|Vasaris]], [[Andalusian Baliscans|Andalusi]], [[Kwangju Baliscans|Kwangju]], [[Zong Baliscans|Zong]], and [[Filipino Baliscans|Maharlikans]].

In 2020, in several barrios of the city, about 60% of the young people under 18 were of [[Kaftia|Kaftian]] or Fosian origin (at least one immigrant parent).
