==Culture and society==
{{Main|Culture of Concepción}}

Concepción is characterized by its culturally rich streetscapes featuring {{W|mixed-use development|mixed-use neighborhoods}} anchored around central commercial corridors to which the {{W|walkability}} of residents and visitors alike is prioritized. Because of these characteristics, Concepción is ranked the "most walkable" city in Balisca. It is recognized as a {{W|world city}} of culture and {{W|creative industries}}. Numerous cultural institutions, many of which enjoy international reputation, are representing the diverse heritage of the city. Many young people, cultural entrepreneurs and international artists continue to settle in the city. Concepción has a vibrant art scene and claims the highest concentration of artists per capita in Balisca. In 2012, Concepción was designated as one of Balisca's top five art communities, recognizing [[Sant Martí]], [[Maleján, Concepción|Maleján]], [[Siétamo]], and [[Biscarrués]] as communities "that have most successfully combined art, artists and venues for creativity and expression with artist collectives, artisan cooperatives and pop-ups (including [[W:Pop-up restaurant|restaurants]], [[W:Pop-up retail|shops]], and [[W:Pop-up exhibition|exhibitions]]) lifestyle to make vibrant neighborhoods."

Concepción is currently at the leading edge of the global contemporary art scene. There are over 1000 art galleries in the city. It is estimated that 6,000 to 7,000 artists live in the city, with a third of them being from outside Balisca. The beginnings of the modern boom in Concepción's art scene were during the 1980s. Concepción is home to a large array of public artworks, statues and sculptures, including {{W|street installations}}. Sculptors such as [[tba]] have played a large part in enhancing many of the city's public spaces with their iconic and larger-than-life works. In more modern times, the city has become well known for {{W|stencil graffiti}} and other {{W|street art}} that appears in the city's numerous throughways.

Concepción's nightlife is one of the most diverse and vibrant of its kind in the [[Algarves]]. Throughout the 1990s, people in their twenties from many countries, particularly those in the [[Northern Hemisphere]], have made Concepción's club scene the premier nightlife destination of the continent. After the [[October 76]] events and [[Special Period|subsequent economic recession]], many historic buildings in [[El Pobleno]], the former city center, were occupied and re-purposed by young {{W|squatters|squatters}} and became a fertile ground for [[autonomous commune (Balisca)|underground]] and [[Desconexión|counterculture]] gatherings. Concepción is additionally notable for the length of its parties. Clubs are not required to close at a fixed time on the weekends, and many parties last well into the morning, or all weekend.
